sanctioned: Go backend codegen bug for a function value boxed through `Ok`/`Just` (the same `any`-typed-carrier class documented in function_payload_gate and ctor_decl_fn_payload, where Go's generated code cannot correctly call an `interface{}`-boxed function). Here it does not hard-fail `go build` — it silently computes the WRONG result: `Just (\x -> x * 2) |> Maybe.andMap (Just 21)` should be `Just 42` per `Ipe.Core.Maybe.andMap`'s own definition (`Just (fn a)`), but the compiled Go binary prints `21` (`ma` passed through unchanged, the function never actually invoked). Verified directly against `/usr/local/bin/ipe` (v0.16.29) with an unambiguous named-function probe on the `Result` sibling (`Ok addTen |> Result.andMap (Ok 5)` with `addTen x = x + 10`): Go prints `5`, not the correct `15` — same bug class, both `Maybe`/`Result` share the same Go codegen path. Rust's `Box<dyn Fn>` kernel call (`maybe_and_map`) computes the semantically correct value. Divergence from Ipe, rationale: Go backend bug (not a Ipe behavior choice).
